KZ3 patch 2044 (RSX pass 44): an A8R8G8B8 read of a Z24S8 zeta takes the zeta when its depth is newer than the
last real colour write to the colour surface at the same address.
rsx_live_draw.c: surfaces record colour_gen (draws whose colour mask is not all zero, per MRT nibble, and colour
clears) and zetas zwrite_gen (depth test+write draws) on one counter, g_ld_cw_gen. At the texture bind, a
ZALIAS_ARGB read (patch 2011 byte rebuild) whose zeta holds depth (had_write or a valid snapshot: had_write is
cleared once a snapshot is taken) newer than every colour alias' colour_gen skips the colour alias, as patch 2022
already did for X16/DEPTH16 reads. Cause in KZ3: from level 2 on, the depth pre-pass binds the scene zeta's address
0x25C0000 as its colour target with all channels masked; the black colour alias won the bind, the half-res depth
downsample (SHADER_CONTROL 0x300840E) rebuilt depth 0 everywhere, the DoF depth 0x1A1C000 went flat at 4.88e-5
(near) and DepthToFuzzy blurred the whole frame. LD_NO_ZETA_ARGB_PREFER=1 = old behaviour. Logs: [zeta-argb]
(decision changes, the first colour writes into zeta addresses, and with LD_ZPROBE the per-bind decision).
Diagnostic: LD_DRAW_INPUTS=0:<idx>,... (patch 2043) = the first full frame after the gated LD_DRAW_DUMP frame.
Host test tools/smoke/test_zeta_argb.c. Upstream candidate (general aliasing rule).

